  "name": "Gamad (Padang coastal song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song genre of the Minangkabau west coast, centred on Padang, that grew from the acculturation of Minang pantun singing with Western music, a history local writers trace to the Portuguese presence on the coast from the sixteenth century; the name is often derived from gamit, to touch someone to draw their attention. Pantun verses sung in Minang are accompanied by violin, accordion, guitar, bass, a gendang drum and a tambourine-like frame drum (the generic frame-drum card stands in).",
